 joining us today is civil rights  attorney jeffrey storms and terry austin  terry this is a great result for the  mclean family what do you think this  means for the family and the city of  aurora  well for the family brian nothing is  going to bring elijah back and it is  such a horrific case he's innocent  walking down the street literally  minding his own business and he is  basically attacked and held down and  then had this ketamine put into his  system and it was way too much and  clearly it caused his death i think the  settlement will help the family with the  pain and suffering that they are going  through and clearly they are going  through severe pain and suffering over  his death  the amount of the settlement has not  been announced as you mentioned and  that's probably because it's got to be  approved by the authorities we may hear  the amount after that authority has  basically approved it and as for the  allocation clearly we have to wait to  see what's going to happen some of it  will be allocated between the mother and  the father and so that has to be ironed  out and my thought ryan is that some of  this money like we've seen in other  civil rights settlements may actually go  back to the city to do some programs  absolutely jeffrey on a more macro level  do you think this settlement like the  floyd settlement you helped obtain is  furthering a momentum to better policing  especially concerning issues of mental  health  brian it's definitely one part of the  puzzle and as terry mentioned we don't  know what the amount is yet but i think  with respect to that piece of the puzzle  the settlement has to be significant  enough  that it makes administrators uh  politicians  understand that they need to enforce  training and they need to enforce  discipline to prevent this the other  piece of the puzzle that's really  critical are the criminal charges that  these individuals  because uh the criminal piece reminds  the officers that hey the city is not  going to just buy you out of this  your freedom your liberty is at  issue if you do not follow the law when  you're performing your job absolutely  just another piece of the puzzle as you  perfectly put there jeff we'll see how  those pieces fall into place as this  case progresses on update now on a story  we first brought you earlier in the week  the so-called january 6 committee votes  to hold former trump adviser steve  bannon in criminal contempt  on tuesday the committee unanimously  passed a criminal contempt report on  thursday the house will vote on a  contempt of congress resolution all this  is in relation to the capital riots that  happened on january 6th the house select  committee in charge of investigating the  january 6 attacks requested bannon  provided details about conversations he  had with former president donald trump  they say those conversations happened  leading up to the riots bannon refused  to provide the information and didn't  show up after being subpoenaed on monday  former president trump filed a lawsuit  to stop the january 6 committee from  obtaining his records  when we come back the latest in jury  selection for the death of a mont arbory  trial how many of the hundreds called to  serve will move on to the next round of  questions and what attorneys look for in  potential jurors next  welcome back jury selection stretches  into day three in georgia as a death of  a mod arbory trial is underway before  the trial can begin 12 jurors must be  seated along with four alternates jury  duty notices were mailed to a thousand  people in the brunswick georgia area  with 600 people called to appear  starting on monday all this as three  georgia men face charges of malice  murder felony murder and other related  charges in the death of 25 year old  ahmad arbury in february 2020 aubry was  shot and killed while jogging near his  brunswick georgia home he was unarmed at  the time of his death father and son duo  gregory and travis mcmichael tailed  aubry in a pickup truck before travis  mcmichael shot and killed him the pair  claimed self-defense and planned to cite  a georgia citizen's arrest law that has  since been repealed and replaced the  mcmichael's neighbor william bryan  followed along in his truck capturing  the entire incident on his cell phone  the shooting created national outrage  after the cell phone video went viral in  may of last year after that gregory and  travis mcmichael were arrested followed  by brian's arrest two weeks later all  three men have pled not guilty to the  charges on wednesday judge timothy  walmsley addressed potential jurors  first the state and then the defense in  this room are going to be asking you  what we call general  questions those general questions are  intended to help the lawyers determine  whether or not  you can be a fair unbiased impartial  juror that is honestly seeking the truth  in this case that effectively that you  will be able to listen to the evidence  presented in the superior court  and be able to make a decision reach a  verdict based upon the evidence  presented  jeffrey you represented the floyd family  and currently represent the parents of  dante wright what do you think the  aubrey family is going through right now  during jury selection  you know that now that we're a little  deeper into brian i think the family  starts to see what a grind this process  is initially you know for the first uh  initial jurors you're you're amped up  you're emotional it's setting in that  you know that some of these individuals  may be deciding one of the most  important things that's happened in your  lifetime uh and so  so you have that but then you just see  how long this takes and you know as that  process wears on the things that really  stand out to you or how frightening some  of these potential jurors really can be  and how relieved you are they're not on  your jury uh but at this point of time  i'm sure it's really wearing on the  family the leng